% Context
% Inspired by the following dataset , we have a collection of data on the first 15 minutes of about 50000 Diamond ranked League of Legends matches scraped using Riot's API. 
% Can you predict their outcomes?
% Content
% Data
% All matches were collected with the following parameters:
% Season: 13
% Server: NA1
% Rank: Diamond
% Tier: I,II,III,IV
% Acknowledgements
% Thank you to Riot Games for allowing access to their API.
% Inspiration
% When working on the linked dataset above, we see classification accuracy peak around 70. Given that we have 5 times the amount of data, I wanted to explore how this would improve our results.
@RELATION League-of-Legends-Diamond-Games-(First-15-Minutes)

@ATTRIBUTE Unnamed:_0 INTEGER
@ATTRIBUTE matchId REAL
@ATTRIBUTE blue_win INTEGER
@ATTRIBUTE blueGold REAL
@ATTRIBUTE blueMinionsKilled REAL
@ATTRIBUTE blueJungleMinionsKilled REAL
@ATTRIBUTE blueAvgLevel REAL
@ATTRIBUTE redGold REAL
@ATTRIBUTE redMinionsKilled REAL
@ATTRIBUTE redJungleMinionsKilled REAL
@ATTRIBUTE redAvgLevel REAL
@ATTRIBUTE blueChampKills REAL
@ATTRIBUTE blueHeraldKills REAL
@ATTRIBUTE blueDragonKills REAL
@ATTRIBUTE blueTowersDestroyed REAL
@ATTRIBUTE redChampKills REAL
@ATTRIBUTE redHeraldKills REAL
@ATTRIBUTE redDragonKills REAL
@ATTRIBUTE redTowersDestroyed REAL

